*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 4~16.67 seconds<sup>120f~500f</sup>.
*4 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*5 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage's Dark enemies are no longer particularly threatening. This stage aims to prevent [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] from blocking the Two Cans' waves by using Dark Otta along side the Two Cans, potentially shredding your Octo.

However, there is an enemy that greatly helps here: Wall Doge. By not killing Wall Doge too quickly, Octopus will avoid getting hit by the Dark Otters and Two Cans, keeping it alive. You can then stack units like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Rugby Cat (Rare Cat)|Gridiron Cat]] alongside [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] to deal huge amounts of damage.

When your units reach the SLOTH, you should summon [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] with units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to rush him down. Even if he doesn't die in the first cycle, you can just wait for Bahamut to recharge.

